  "Question": "If \\(A * B\\) means \\(\\dfrac{A + B}{2},\\) then \\((3 * 5) * 8\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(12\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(30\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The parentheses tell us to calculate \\(3*5\\) first. The given rule takes half the sum of its two inputs, so\n\\[\n3*5=\\frac{3+5}{2}=4.\n\\]\nUse \\(4\\) as the first input in the next operation:\n\\[\n(3*5)*8=4*8=\\frac{4+8}{2}=6.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(6\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
